\\sin\\theta$#2. The Real Meaning of $e^x$ — the $\\exp(x)$ Function#2.3 Computing values — sanity check *(at [[10:00]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZxYOEwM6Wbk&t=600s))*#{5}":[92,93],"#Euler's Formula via $\\exp(x)$ — Why $e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$#2. The Real Meaning of $e^x$ — the $\\exp(x)$ Function#2.4 The defining property: $\\exp(a+b) = \\exp(a)\\exp(b)$ *(formalized at [[14:46]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZxYOEwM6Wbk&t=886s))*":[94,112],"#Euler's Formula via $\\exp(x)$ — Why $e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$#2. The Real Meaning of $e^x$ — the $\\exp(x)$ Function#2.4 The defining property: $\\exp(a+b) = \\exp(a)\\exp(b)$ *(formalized at [[14:46]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZxYOEwM6Wbk&t=886s))*#{1}":[96,112],"#Euler's Formula via $\\exp(x)$ — Why $e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$#2. The Real Meaning of $e^x$ — the $\\exp(x)$ Function#2.5 Why $\\exp(0) = 1$ *(at [[27:44]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZxYOEwM6Wbk&t=1664s))*":[113,123],"#Euler's Formula via $\\exp(x)$ — Why $e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$#2. The Real Meaning of $e^x$ — the $\\exp(x)$ Function#2.5 Why $\\exp(0) = 1$ *(at [[27:44]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZxYOEwM6Wbk&t=1664s))*#{1}":[115,123],"#Euler's Formula via $\\exp(x)$ — Why $e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$#2. The Real Meaning of $e^x$ — the $\\exp(x)$ Function#2.6 Worked: deriving $\\exp(5) = e^5$, $\\exp(-1) = 1/e$, $\\exp(1/2) = \\sqrt{e}$ *(at [[20:34]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZxYOEwM6Wbk&t=1234s))*":[124,162],"#Euler's Formula via $\\exp(x)$ — Why $e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$#2. The Real Meaning of $e^x$ — the $\\exp(x)$ Function#2.6 Worked: deriving $\\exp(5) = e^5$, $\\exp(-1) = 1/e$, $\\exp(1/2) = \\sqrt{e}$ *(at [[20:34]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZxYOEwM6Wbk&t=1234s))*#{1}":[126,162],"#Euler's Formula via $\\exp(x)$ — Why $e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$#3. The Spiral — How $\\exp(i\\theta)$ Walk